@startuml
title Sequence Diagram - UC-14 - Block Distracting Application

autonumber
participant "DetectDistractionUseCase" as DetectUseCase
participant "BlockDistractionUseCase" as UseCase
participant "DistractionBlockerPort" as Blocker
participant "Operating System" as OS
participant "TransactionalOutbox" as Events
participant "Outbox Dispatcher" as Dispatcher
participant "DistractionLogProjection" as LogProjection
participant "SessionWebSocketHandler" as WS

DetectUseCase -> UseCase : block(command{detectionId, app})
UseCase -> Blocker : block(app)
Blocker -> OS : request application block
OS --> Blocker : BlockingResult

Blocker --> UseCase : BlockingResult.success()
UseCase -> Events : appendToOutbox(DistractionBlocked)
Events -> LogProjection : onDistractionBlocked(event)
activate LogProjection
LogProjection -> LogProjection : markBlocked(detectionId)
deactivate LogProjection
Dispatcher -> WS : broadcast("distraction.blocked")
WS --> DetectUseCase : distraction.blocked\n{detectionId, blockedAt}
UseCase --> DetectUseCase : DistractionDto{blocked: true}

note over Blocker, OS
  Platform-specific adapters:
  - Windows: process suspend / foreground window
  - macOS: NSWorkspace / Accessibility APIs
  - Linux: X11 / Wayland compositor hooks
end note

note over Events, Dispatcher
  Events commit atomically with the aggregate; the dispatcher
  delivers them only after commit and retries failed consumers.
end note

note over LogProjection
  The DistractionLog is a read model. The block use
  case publishes the outcome; it never updates the
  log repository directly.
end note

@enduml
